  "summary": "ps-bool executes an opaque base85+zlib payload on import",
  "details": "The package ships a single module main.py whose entire body is exec(zlib.decompress(base64.b85decode('...'))) — an opaque obfuscated blob decoded and executed in-process at import time. setup.py registers a console_script entry point 'psbool = main:main', so both importing the module and invoking the installed CLI trigger the exec. PKG-INFO contains only Name and Version with no description, author, homepage, or declared purpose, and no readable source is shipped. This is the canonical PyPI dropper shape: decode-and-exec of an opaque payload with no legitimate functionality visible in source and no declared purpose to anchor a benign explanation.",
